{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-gen-17-1","title":"Genesis 17:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 God renews the covenant with Abram, and changes his name to Abraham, in token of a greater blessing. 9 Circumcision is instituted. 15 Sarai's name is changed to Sarah, and she is blessed. 17 Isaac is promised, and the time of his birth fixed. 23 Abraham and Ishmael are circumcised.</p>\n<p>A.M. 2107. B.C. 1897. was. 16:16 the Lord. 12:1 Almighty. 18:14; 28:3; 35:11; Ex 6:3; Nu 11:23; De 10:17; Job 11:7; Ps 115:3 Jer 32:17; Da 4:35; Mt 19:26; Eph 3:20; Php 4:13; Heb 7:25 walk. 5:22,24; 6:9; 48:15; 1Ki 2:4; 3:6; 8:25; 2Ki 20:3; Ps 116:9; Isa 38:3 Mic 6:8; Lu 1:6; Ac 23:1; 24:16; Heb 12:28 perfect. or, upright, or sincere. 6:9; De 18:13; Job 1:1; Mt 5:48</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-2","title":"Genesis 17:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>And I. 4-6; 9:9; 15:18; Ps 105:8-11; Ga 3:17,18 multiply. 12:2; 13:16; 22:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-3","title":"Genesis 17:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>17; Ex 3:6; Le 9:23,24; Nu 14:5; 16:22,45; Jos 5:14; Jud 13:20 1Ki 18:39; Eze 1:28; 3:23; 9:8; Da 8:17,18; 10:9; Mt 17:6; Re 1:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-4","title":"Genesis 17:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>a father. 12:2; 13:16; 16:10; 22:17; 25:1-18; 32:12; 35:11; 36:1-43; Nu 1:1-54 Nu 26:1-65; Ro 4:11-18; Ga 3:28,29 many nations. Heb. multitude of nations.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-5","title":"Genesis 17:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>but thy name. 15; 32:28; Nu 13:16; 2Sa 12:25; Ne 9:7; Isa 62:2-4; 65:15; Jer 20:3 Jer 23:6; Mt 1:21-23; Joh 1:42; Re 2:17 Abraham. i.e., father of a great multitude.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-6","title":"Genesis 17:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>nations. 4,20; 35:11 kings. 16; 36:31-43; Ezr 4:20; Mt 1:6-17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-7","title":"Genesis 17:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>And I. 15:18; 26:24; Ex 6:4; Ps 105:8-11; Mic 7:20; Lu 1:54,55,72-75 Ro 9:4,8,9; Ga 3:17; Eph 2:2 God. 26:24; 28:13; Ex 3:6,15; Le 26:12; Ps 81:10; Eze 28:26; Mt 22:32 Heb 8:10; 11:16 and to. Ex 19:5,6; Mr 10:14; Ac 2:39; Ro 9:7-9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-8","title":"Genesis 17:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>And I. 12:7; 13:15,17; 15:7-21; Ps 105:9,11 wherein thou art a stranger. Heb. of thy sojournings. 23:4; 28:4 everlasting. 48:4; Ex 21:6; 31:16,17; 40:15; Le 16:34; Nu 25:13; De 32:8; 2Sa 23:5 Ps 103:17; Heb 9:15 their. Ex 6:7; Le 26:12; De 4:37; 14:2; 26:18; 29:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-9","title":"Genesis 17:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Ps 25:10; 103:18; Isa 56:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-10","title":"Genesis 17:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Every. 11; 34:15; Ex 4:25; 12:48; De 10:16; 30:6; Jos 5:2,4; Jer 4:4; 9:25,26 Ac 7:8; Ro 2:28,29; 3:1,25,28,30; 4:9-11; 1Co 7:18,19; Ga 3:28 Ga 5:3-6; 6:12; Eph 2:11; Php 3:3; Col 2:11,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-11","title":"Genesis 17:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>the flesh. Ex 4:25; Jos 5:3; 1Sa 18:25-27; 2Sa 3:14 a token. Ac 7:8; Ro 4:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-12","title":"Genesis 17:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>he that is eight days old. Heb. a son of eight days. 21:4; Le 12:3; Lu 1:59; 2:21; Joh 7:22,23; Ac 7:8; Ro 2:28; Php 3:5 is born. 23; Ex 12:48,49</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-13","title":"Genesis 17:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>born. 14:14; 15:3; Ex 12:44; 21:4 bought. 37:27,36; 39:1; Ex 21:2,16; Ne 5:5,8; Mt 18:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-14","title":"Genesis 17:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>cut. Ex 4:24-26; 12:15,19; 30:33,38; Le 7:20,21,25,27; 18:29; 19:8 Nu 15:30,31; Jos 5:2-12 broken. Ps 55:20; Isa 24:5; 33:8; Jer 11:10; 31:32; 1Co 11:27,29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-15","title":"Genesis 17:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>As. 5; 32:28; 2Sa 12:25 Sarah. i.e., princess.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-16","title":"Genesis 17:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>And I. 1:28; 12:2; 24:60; Ro 9:9 give. 18:10-14 be a mother of nations. Heb. become nations. 35:11; Ga 4:26-31; 1Pe 3:6 kings. 6; Isa 49:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-17","title":"Genesis 17:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>fell. 3; Le 9:24; Nu 14:5; 16:22,45; De 9:18,25; Jos 5:14; 7:6; Jud 13:20 1Ch 21:16; Job 1:20; Eze 1:28; Da 8:17; Mt 2:11; Re 5:8; 11:16 laughed. 18:12; 21:6; Joh 8:56; Ro 4:19,20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-18","title":"Genesis 17:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>O that. Jer 32:39; Ac 2:39 before. 4:12,14; Ps 4:6; 41:12; Isa 59:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-19","title":"Genesis 17:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Sarah. 21; 18:10-14; 21:2,3,6; 2Ki 4:16,17; Lu 1:13-20; Ro 9:6-9; Ga 4:28-31 Isaac.{Yitzchak,} which we change into Isaac, signifies laughter; in allusion to Abraham's laughing, ver. 17. By this Abraham did not express his unbelief or weakness of faith, but his joy at the prospect of the fulfilment of so glorious a promise; and to this our Lord evidently alludes, Joh 8:56.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-20","title":"Genesis 17:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>I have blessed. 16:10-12 twelve. 25:12-18 and I. 21:13,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-21","title":"Genesis 17:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>my. 21:10-12; 26:2-5; 46:1; 48:15; Ex 2:24; 3:6; Lu 1:55,72; Ro 9:5,6,9 Ga 3:29; Heb 11:9 at. 18:10; 21:2,3; Job 14:13; Ac 1:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-22","title":"Genesis 17:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>3; 18:33; 35:9-15; Ex 20:22; Nu 12:6-8; De 5:4; Jud 6:21; 13:20 Joh 1:18; 10:30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-23","title":"Genesis 17:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>circumcised. 10-14,26,27; 18:19; 34:24; Jos 5:2-9; Ps 119:60; Pr 27:1; Ec 9:10 Ac 16:3; Ro 2:25-29; 4:9-12; 1Co 7:18,19; Ga 5:6; 6:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-24","title":"Genesis 17:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>1,17; 12:4; Ro 4:11,19,20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-25","title":"Genesis 17:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>Not only the Jews, but the Arabs, who are the descendants of Ishmael, retain the rite of circumcision to this day; and the latter perform it, as the other Mahometanus also do, at the age of thirteen.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-26","title":"Genesis 17:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>12:4; 22:3,4; Ps 119:60</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-17-27","title":"Genesis 17:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>circumcised. 18:19</p>"}]}